# DTF tier manifest: inline-scan-proxy-pypi-2954  (#2954)
# Profile-set: filesystem + trivy scanner. Needs the bundled Grype engine
# (seeded CVE-DB, shipped in the runtime image) AND outbound access to
# pypi.org to fetch the probe wheels. The scanners.trivy profile stands up the
# scanner-adapter for parity with production; Grype is the effective CVE engine
# for filesystem wheels and runs from the bundled binary regardless — the
# fail-closed verdict here is produced by Grype.
#
# WHAT IT GUARDS (#2954, Part 2 — PyPI proxy scan-on-fetch-and-block):
#   Proxy-cached bytes are deliberately not written to `artifacts` (#1278/#1280),
#   so the artifact_id-keyed scanner pipeline never scanned them: `scan_on_proxy`
#   was a pure log warning (#1274) and a vulnerable wheel streamed straight
#   through (200) on the very first `pip install`. The fix runs the leaf Grype
#   scanner over the buffered upstream bytes (new ScannerService::scan_content
#   over a synthetic in-memory Artifact, no DB row), persists a digest-keyed
#   verdict (`proxy_scan_results`, migration 181), and blocks fail-closed.
#
# Discriminating oracle (oracle.sh), fail-closed:
#   * CVE wheel (Jinja2-2.10-py2.py3-none-any.whl, Grype flags CVE-2019-10906 /
#     CVE-2020-28493) GET ->
#       Fixed (#2954):   403 scan_blocked, AND a `vulnerable` proxy_scan_results
#                        row for its digest, AND a REPEAT GET is still 403
#                        served from the verdict cache with NO second Grype scan
#                        (no upstream re-fetch).
#       Pre-#2954:       200 (unscanned wheel streamed through) -> FAIL.
#   * Clean wheel (six-1.16.0-py2.py3-none-any.whl) GET -> 200 with
#     `X-AK-Scan: clean` on BOTH images (pins that the gate only blocks
#     vulnerable content).
#   * CVE-engine-error discriminator: with Grype rendered non-functional (its
#     binary swapped for an exit-1 stub), a fail-closed pull of a FRESH CVE
#     wheel (PyYAML-5.3.1) ->
#       Fixed:     423 (inconclusive), NO `clean` row persisted, and a re-pull
#                  after Grype is restored RE-SCANS and 403s.
#       Pre-fix:   200 (the always-on DependencyScanner's Ok(empty) on a binary
#                  wheel masks the Grype error -> aggregates to `clean`), and a
#                  poisoned `clean` row keeps it 200 even after Grype recovers.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: admin login + repo/config setup + several proxy
# pulls back-to-back.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem scanners.trivy"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
NEEDS_INTERNET="true"
